GridSFM: vendored third-party code
==================================

Source:   https://github.com/microsoft/GridSFM
Commit:   1ca775fd436d7ce013a1c0ab946e61ac7ef59ad6
Package:  gridsfm 1.1.0 (the repository's model/gridsfm/ directory)
License:  MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation; see LICENSE here.

Vendored unmodified (byte-identical to the commit above):

  blocks.py  checkpoint.py  cycle_basis.py  data.py  dc_prior.py  eval.py
  finetune_opfdata.py  hodge_pe.py  loss.py  model.py  pe_features.py
  schema.py  signed_incidence.py  stress_features.py  synthetic.py

Not vendored: opfdata_train.py (it wraps the OPFData downloader; the Table 1 corpus
is not OPFData), hf_util/, and upstream's package __init__.py. The __init__.py in
this directory is a replacement that re-exports only names from the modules present;
it is the only file here not taken from upstream.

What uses it:

  powerform/model/baselines/gridsfm.py
    * the decision row: GridTransformerBackbone with its Pg and V heads read as the
      two decisions (p_g, vm_set) and its theta, Qg and feasibility heads deleted,
      trained with the decision recipe;
    * the state-regression row: the stock backbone from random init, trained with
      GridSFM's own fine-tuning recipe (finetune_opfdata, compute_loss,
      SyntheticMixedDataset) and scored on the state it emits.

Runtime dependencies (not vendored): torch, torch_geometric, numpy, scipy,
huggingface_hub (imported by checkpoint.py).

cycle_basis.CycleBasisCache writes a small disk cache under $XDG_CACHE_HOME (default
~/.cache); set XDG_CACHE_HOME to keep it elsewhere.
